{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-28T16:11:10.969Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"738f7d9b84aae278517b105a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1603","claim:pm-gh1617","lineage:pm-gh1603","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1603+pm-gh1617","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1603","claim:pm-gh1617","lineage:pm-gh1603","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1618"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1618: prevent automated comment churn from misleading next-work priority"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"**Version:** pm 2026.10.28, a real tracker with 112 next candidates (90 ready). `pm next --help` says: *\"Answers 'what should I work on now?' with the highest-priority ready item\"*.\n\n**Observed:** the recommendation is a **P2** task, an append-only automation audit log (\"Hosted auto-update runs … Never close this item\"). A host cron appends one comment to it every hour; it has 161 comments. Two **P0** issues, both open, unblocked and unassigned, rank 9th and 17th, behind six P1 items.\n\n`pm next --json --explain-ranking` shows why:\n\n| id | priority | baseline_rank | final rank | recency | activity_density | priority_pressure |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| audit-log task | P2 | 35 | **1** | 0.342 (hourly `comment_add`, classed `substantive`) | **0.25** | 0.175 |\n| P1 feature | P1 | 11 | 2 | 0.291 | 0.030 | 0.262 |\n| P0 issue | P0 | — | 9 | — | — | — |\n\n`recency` takes its coordinate from the latest `comment_add`, classed `event_class: substantive`. `activity_density` counts comments. So machine-written log comments outweigh priority, and a P0 incident loses to a log that grows by itself.\n\n**Why it matters for agents:** an agent that follows `pm next` (the documented \"what now?\" entry point) works on the wrong item and never gets to the P0 work. It also costs a second query and manual re-ranking to notice. Any tracker with an automation that comments regularly (CI receipts, updater runs, sync bots) has the same problem.\n\n**Expected (any of these would fix it):**\n1. Treat priority as a floor: a ready P0 always ranks above ready P1/P2 unless a caller-declared intent says otherwise. The help text promises this.\n2. Don't count automated or append-only comment churn as substantive recency or activity. For example, classify comments by `author_source` / harness, or let an item be declared non-actionable/log so it never becomes `recommended`.\n3. In the default (non-explain) output, give the reason a lower-priority item outranks a higher-priority one (`reasons` currently shows just `p2`), so an agent can see why the recommendation isn't the highest priority.\n\nRelated: #513 (ready queue not priority-ordered, closed). This is the scorer variant of it: the queue is now ranked, but by signals that automation can inflate.\n\n\nIntake only: reproduce against the current public SDK before selecting a ranking policy. Preserve custom project scoring and explicit intent while reconciling the default recommendation with its documented priority contract."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","context","github","ranking","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-28T16:11:10.969Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-28T16:11:10.969Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Reproduce a ready P0 population competing with automated P2 comment churn;Define explicit default and caller-customizable ranking policy;Verify explanations and SDK CLI MCP parity with bounded token costs"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-4k6b"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Default next-work advice cannot silently elevate an automated P2 log above ready P0 work; documented policy and ranking explanations match tested behavior."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-07pt16","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-28T16:11:10.969Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-1mwk","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-28T16:11:10.969Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:11:10.969Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: complete initial strict3146-item all-status corpus plus fresh specific searches and open/in-progress inventories found no existing owner for GH1618. Read full live pm-4k6b and completed pm-1mwk/pm-07pt16 lineage. This new report arrived during PR1619 validation and remains open/unclaimed; no reproduction or fix is asserted."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b5a731d9b52fd9a383161a2d48be19666ea8bd0e4c7d6af770a1a66d7fb02336","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_vers