{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T02:23:26.465Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"fe411f5ac7c0c68c436d07f8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-4k6b","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-gh1618","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-4k6b","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T02:23:26.465Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reproduced on current source. The default scorer (default-weighted-v1) blends ten signals; priority_pressure carries about 11% of the normalizing weight while recency, activity_density and knowledge_density (all raised by comment_add events, which event classification treats as substantive regardless of author) carry about 27%, so a P2 item with steady comment churn can outscore ready P0/P1 work. There is no automation marker on comments or history (author_source/agent_harness only), and no settings key influenced the order. Real-tracker evidence (229 open, 112 ready, pm next --limit 5 --explain-ranking): under the blended order a P2 chore with activity_density 0.233 and recency 0.294 (baseline rank 38) ranks 5th above P1 items; under the new default priority floor it drops below every P1 and rank 5 becomes a P1 (baseline 20). An isolated-tracker test seeds a P2 log with 12 comments beside a P1 and a P0: the floor recommends the P0 and ranks [P0, P1, log]; the weighted policy follows the score order and names the passed-over priority in reasons when the log wins."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T02:23:26.465Z"}],"before_hash":"e3ef73fb7a060a9f3b2e176d84b00938054605cfecdb6b24f61f6c856a750fcc","after_hash":"e722abefb5707080198231d813b487ac8c8ff61fae111677fd304788f1603a10","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b8824c12d83e7253dd94e24e467871d3d05306cec9e560bb03c8b5ce2d7f9e10"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T02:23:26.971Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"fe411f5ac7c0c68c436d07f8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-4k6b","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-gh1618","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-gh1618","lineage:pm-4k6b","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T02:23:26.971Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Fix: NextOptions.rankingPolicy and the context.next_ranking_policy setting (pm config project set context_next_ranking_policy weighted) select priority_floor (default) or weighted. priority_floor reorders only the built-in weighted model's output: in-progress work first (the documented resume contract), then priority tiers, relevance order inside a tier; an extension context_relevance scorer keeps its own order under either policy. filters.ranking_policy discloses the policy on CLI, SDK and MCP; the recommendation reasons add 'priority floor (relevance rank N)' or 'relevance over pN ready work' when policy and score disagree; --explain-ranking keeps each item's score beside its final rank. An unknown policy refuses as invalid_argument_value listing the accepted values. The agent-task token baseline moved by the 10 tokens the new filters field costs on the next step (722 to 732); token-budget, context-intent calibration, refusal-closure, docs-skills, static quality, contra